317,1502,20912,32,73315,362,11,13387,317,1502,20912,33,73315,425,11,41074,317,1502,20912,34,73315,356,11,7856,317,1502,20912,35,73315,422,11,5052,317,12670,468,11,434,280,36,284,320,19,13,20,14523,17,11,16,14523,17,1215,434,284,320,20,11,220,18,317,7633,4346,313,36,313,35,1215,4038,4346,313,37,313,35,317,1502,20912,36,73315,468,11,451,1215,2383,20912,37,73315,434,11,41074,317,16119,4346,1215,16119,5349,1215,16119,3025,1215,16119,5432,1215,16119,10722,1215,16119,7832,317,1502,20912,87,73315,320,16,11,220,16,13,20,701,328,1215,2383,20912,87,73315,320,17,11,220,16,701,328,97883,1215,2383,20912,87,73315,320,17,11,481,16,701,451,71722,71722,97883,317,1502,20912,88,73315,320,20,13,20,48920,18,11,659,20,14523,18,701,328,1215,2383,20912,88,73315,320,21,13,20,48920,18,11,220,15,5905,2383,20912,88,73315,320,20,48920,20,11,481,16,13,20,48920,18,1106,1502,20912,16,16,15,61,35702,43298,31716,44970,17,13,20,11,18,13,20,5905,2383,20912,16,15,15,61,35702,43298,31716,44970,21,13,20,14523,17,11,18,13,20,1106,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nIn quadrilateral $ABCD$, angle $BAD$ and angle $CDA$ are trisected as shown. What is the degree measure of angle $AFD$?\n\n[asy]\nsize(150);\npair A , B, C, D; A = (0,0); B = (2, 4); C = (7,4); D = (7, -2);\ndraw( (0,0)--(2,4) -- (7,4) -- (7, -2)-- cycle);\nlabel(\"$A$\", A, SW);\nlabel(\"$B$\", B, NW);\nlabel(\"$C$\", C, NE);\nlabel(\"$D$\", D, SE);\npair E, F;\nE = (4.5-.2,1-.2); F = (5, 3);\ndraw(A--E--D); draw(A--F--D);\nlabel(\"$E$\", E, N); label(\"$F$\", F, NW);\ndot(A);dot(B);dot(C);dot(D);dot(E);dot(F);\nlabel(\"$x$\", (1, 1.5), S); label(\"$x$\", (2, 1), S+W); label(\"$x$\", (2, -1), N+N+N+W);\nlabel(\"$y$\", (5.5+.3, .5-.3), S); label(\"$y$\", (6.5+.3, 0)); label(\"$y$\", (5+.5, -1.5+.3));\nlabel(\"$110^{\\circ}$\",(2.5,3.5)); label(\"$100^{\\circ}$\",(6.5-.2,3.5));\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"f00cfcb8cfd2c96605522b067b790f8f5ac29f62a2f95bc1c559688fa1720255"},"seconds":18.994780778884888,"seed":435783228305653042,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for the measure of angle \\( \\angle AFD \\), we need to carefully analyze the given information and use the properties of angles in a quadrilateral and angle trisection.\n\n1. **Identify the given angles:**\n   - \\( \\angle BAD = 110^\\circ \\)\n   - \\( \\angle CDA = 100^\\circ \\)\n\n2. **Trisect the angles:**\n   - Since \\( \\angle BAD \\) is trisected, each of the three angles is:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{110^\\circ}{3} \\approx 36.67^\\circ\n     \\]\n   - Similarly, since \\( \\angle CDA \\) is trisected, each of the three angles is:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{100^\\circ}{3} \\approx 33.33^\\circ\n     \\]\n\n3. **Label the trisected angles:**\n   - Let \\( \\angle BAE = \\angle EAF = \\angle FDA = 36.67^\\circ \\)\n   - Let \\( \\angle DCF = \\angle FCD = \\angle FDC = 33.33^\\circ \\)\n\n4. **Sum of angles in quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\):**\n   - The sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral is \\(360^\\circ\\).\n\n5. **Sum of angles at point \\(A\\):**\n   - Since \\( \\angle BAE \\) and \\( \\angle EAF \\) are adjacent angles at \\(A\\), and \\( \\angle DAF \\) is the remaining part of \\( \\angle BAD \\):\n     \\[\n     \\angle BAE + \\angle EAF + \\angle DAF = 110^\\circ\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     36.67^\\circ + 36.67^\\circ + 36.67^\\circ = 110^\\circ\n     \\]\n\n6. **Sum of angles at point \\(D\\):**\n   - Similarly, since \\( \\angle DCF \\) and \\( \\angle FCD \\) are adjacent angles at \\(D\\), and \\( \\angle FDA \\) is the remaining part of \\( \\angle CDA \\):\n     \\[\n     \\angle DCF + \\angle FCD + \\angle FDA = 100^\\circ\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     33.33^\\circ + 33.33^\\circ + 33.33^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n     \\]\n\n7. **Calculate \\( \\angle AFD \\):**\n   - Consider the straight line through \\(A\\) and \\(D\\). The sum of the angles on a straight line is \\(180^\\circ\\).\n   - The angles around point \\(F\\) form a straight line:\n     \\[\n     \\angle AFD = 180^\\circ - (\\angle DAF + \\angle FDC)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\angle AFD = 180^\\circ - (36.67^\\circ + 33.33^\\circ)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\angle AFD = 180^\\circ - 70^\\circ\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\angle AFD = 110^\\circ\n     \\]\n\nThus, the degree measure of angle \\( \\angle AFD \\) is \\(\\boxed{110}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{110}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:411"}
